    feeds: ["purpose", "resilience to threat", "coherent life story"],
    description:
      "A meta-analysis of ten prospective studies (136,265 people) found higher purpose in life associated with lower all-cause mortality and fewer cardiovascular events, and purpose predicted survival across adulthood in the MIDUS sample. Self-affirmation research shows that briefly writing about core values buffers threat and can shift behaviour over surprisingly long periods. A validated questionnaire (the MLQ) separates presence of meaning from the search for it. For legacy, values are the spine the stories hang on.",
    action: "Write your five core values on one card today with one sentence each on how they show up in your week; re-write the card every quarter. When a decision feels heavy, re-read the card before deciding — that is the affirmation exercise.",
