    description:
      "The Legacy Project trials paired an ill older adult with a family caregiver and an interventionist (later, trained senior volunteers) across three home visits to create a personal legacy — a scrapbook, a cookbook, audiotaped stories. Every family in the pilot started a project and reported better communication; the randomized trial found greater reductions in patients' emotional symptoms and bother and improved spiritual functioning, and caregivers endorsed more meaning in life. Only one effect persisted after volunteer contact stopped, which is why this is elite: the practice has to keep going, with the volunteers describing it as deeply rewarding for them too.",
    action: "Start one tangible family legacy object this year — a printed family cookbook with a story per recipe, a photo book per decade, or an audio archive — and assign each generation a role. Set a fixed monthly session and a delivery date for the first edition twelve months out, then plan the second.",
